# About Me

:::::: grid
::: g-col-7
Welcome! I am a Ph.D. candidate in political science at the University of California, Los Angeles (UCLA). I study how voters form opinions and how governments translate those opinions into public policy in low-information political environments (particularly U.S. cities).

My research has been funded by the [UCLA Initiative to Study Hate](https://studyofhate.ucla.edu) and the [Graduate Research Mentorship](https://grad.ucla.edu/funding/financial-aid/funding-for-continuing-students/graduate-research-mentorship-program/) fellowship.

## Research Interests

American politics, state/local politics, representation, racial/ethnic politics

